  "id": "COMPOUND:42829 - PROTEIN:522",
  "verbalization": "Deacetylasperuloside appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step mechanism involving the enzyme Threonine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial. The evidence suggests that Deacetylasperuloside acts as a target for two distinct compounds, L-N(omega)-Nitroarginine-2,4-L-diaminobutyric amide and (-)-Valeranone, both of which are known to inhibit Threonine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial. This implies that Deacetylasperuloside may interact with the same target enzyme, potentially through a common pathway or by modulating its activity. The observed scores in the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, suggesting that Deacetylasperuloside may influence the function of Threonine--tRNA ligase, mitochondrial, possibly by affecting the enzyme's activity or stability. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Deacetylasperuloside could play a role in regulating mitochondrial function through its interaction with this critical enzyme.",
